            <ArticleTitle>Assessment of Murine Retinal Function by Electroretinography.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e2218</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.21769/BioProtoc.2218</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The electroretinogram (ERG) is a sensitive and noninvasive method for testing retinal function. In this protocol, we describe a method for performing ERGs in mice. Contact lenses on the mouse cornea measure the electrical response to a light stimulus of photoreceptors and downstream retinal cells, and the collected data are analyzed to evaluate retinal function.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
